      {
        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 10,
        "titulo": "Colours and the adjective after «sein»",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: to describe something with «sein», the adjective comes AFTER the verb and does NOT change: «Die Jacke ist blau», «Die Schuhe sind schwarz». No ending is added, just as in English («blue» for the jacket and for the shoes). STEP 2: ask «Welche Farbe hat …?» (which colour does … have?) or «Wie ist …?». STEP 3: colours are always written in lowercase here, because they are adjectives. STEP 4: the adjective can take «zu» (too): «Die Hose ist zu groß.» The change in the adjective ending (ein blaues Hemd) only comes in A2; for now, use the adjective ALONE, after «sein».",
        "comparacao": "In English the adjective never changes («the blue jacket», «the blue shoes»). In German too, after «sein» it is invariable: «ist blau», «sind blau». The difference only appears later, when the adjective goes before the noun.",
